    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The indicator assesses the total area of catchment land that is effectively protected against further degradation. The protection is ensured by community bylaws, regulations enforced by community members and relevant authorities, individual farmers applying sustainable agricultural practices and other means.

A catchment area of wetlands is an area of land, usually bounded by natural features such as hills or mountains, from which surface and sub-surface water flows into streams, rivers, and wetlands. It is also known as a watershed area, drainage area, drainage basin, basin, or catchment.</narrative>
    </description>
